{
  "manufacturer": "Siemens",
  "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
  "model": "BACnet PTEC VAV Controller - Application 6659 (VAV / Chilled Beam with CO2 Demand Control Ventilation)",
  "model_slug": "ptec-6659-vav-chilled-beam-dcv",
  "short_model": "PTEC VAV Chilled Beam DCV 6659",
  "aliases": [
    "PTEC 6659",
    "Application 6659",
    "App 6659",
    "550-494PA",
    "Siemens chilled beam controller",
    "Siemens VAV demand control ventilation"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "VAV / chilled beam terminal unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Single-duct VAV boxes and active chilled beams with a chilled water valve, a hot water valve and room CO2 demand control ventilation on the Siemens BACnet PTEC controller 550-494PA.",
  "summary": "Application 6659 runs a VAV box or chilled beam on a Siemens BACnet PTEC controller over BACnet MS/TP, with four loops: cooling, heating, airflow and CO2. Airflow and the chilled water valve are sequenced in cooling, airflow and the hot water valve in heating, and each valve can be floating or 0-10 V. When room CO2 rises far enough above outdoor CO2 the box switches to ventilation mode and the coils hold temperature.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "Units are given in US units (°F, cfm, ft²); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
    "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
    "Demand control ventilation is off until CO2 CONFIG (AO 57) is set to 1, 3 or 4; the value picks the CO2 source (room unit or PPCL, AI 3 or AI 4).",
    "MTR SETUP (AO 58) defaults to 0 and must be set to enable the damper motor and any floating valve motors.",
    "DEW POINT and ENTHALPY are calculated only when RH CONFIG (AO 125) selects a humidity source."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet Programmable TEC Controller VAV Chilled Beam with Demand Control Ventilation (CO2) and Floating or Analog Output - Application 6659, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1194",
    "revision_date": "2015-01-09",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/w_zj64eHuf3M_u6_tgTWIw/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing), then release the box to application control. The BMS commands occupancy with DAY.NGT (BO 29) and the day setpoints, and reads room temperature, airflow, valve positions, room CO2 and the error status. For demand control ventilation the field panel writes OUTDOOR CO2; for chilled beams it can close the chilled water valve with CHW DISABLE.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 29",
        "name": "DAY.NGT",
        "why": "DAY = occupied, NIGHT = unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 6",
        "name": "DAY CLG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 7",
        "name": "DAY HTG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 5",
        "name": "HEAT.COOL",
        "why": "Current mode: HEAT or COOL"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "ROOM TEMP",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 35",
        "name": "AIR VOLUME",
        "why": "Measured box airflow, cfm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 39",
        "name": "C VLV POS",
        "why": "Chilled water valve position, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 40",
        "name": "H VLV POS",
        "why": "Hot water valve position, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "RM CO2",
        "why": "Room CO2, ppm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 99",
        "name": "ERROR STATUS",
        "why": "Controller error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Occupancy is DAY.NGT (BO 29). With a wall switch on DI 2 and WALL SWITCH (BO 18) = YES, the switch sets it; standalone with no switch the controller stays in day mode; on a network the field panel or BMS commands DAY.NGT. NGT OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary night override from the room unit button.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "OUTDOOR CO2 (AO 50) has no sensor input; the field panel (PPCL) or an operator must write it for demand control ventilation. RM CO2 can come from the room unit, PPCL or AI 3/AI 4 per CO2 CONFIG. CHW DISABLE (BO 37) = YES from the field panel closes the chilled water valve, e.g. on high dew point.",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the factory value is 255.",
      "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6692."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "As shipped, the controller keeps all equipment OFF until it is released to application control (see Siemens start-up procedures).",
      "Loop gains, motor timing, rotation angles and setup codes are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely.",
      "COND ALM DLY (AO 70) = 0 turns off the DI 6 condensate input; any other value is the alarm delay in seconds before the chilled water valve closes.",
      "Switchover on supply air temperature needs PPCL to command HEAT.COOL (BO 5); the built-in switchover uses only room temperature and loop outputs."
    ]
  },
